"Done — `model_v1.md` is in the workspace. Here's the binding in a nutshell:\n\n**Purpose:** Choose weekly output of A and B to maximize profit without exceeding machine or labor capacity.\n\n**Decision variables:**\n- xA = units of A produced per week\n- xB = units of B produced per week\n\n**Objective:** Maximize weekly profit = 40·xA + 50·xB (USD).\n\n**Constraints:**\n1. Machine: 2·xA + 1·xB ≤ 100 hours/week\n2. Labor: 1·xA + 3·xB ≤ 90 hours/week\n3. xA, xB ≥ 0\n\nI also recorded the assumptions explicitly — most notably **divisibility** (treating units as continuous, i.e. a linear program rather than an integer program) and single-period scope (no demand ceilings or inventory yet). That keeps v1 honest about what it does and doesn't claim.\n\nWant me to solve it next and see what the optimal weekly plan looks like? 🦀"